# RustToBluebookMacrophage — Hecksagon
#
# Infrastructure declaration for the RustToBluebookMacrophage
# aggregate (the imperative-creep immune cell — watches *.rs edits
# and queues bluebook-conversion sidequests). Pairs with
# rust_to_bluebook_macrophage.bluebook.
#
# Phase 1 (i696) : memory adapter only. The aggregate is the
# declared contract ; the substrate that fulfills the contract is
# Phase 2/3 (separate cards) :
#
#   * Phase 2 — PostToolUse hook on Edit/Write/MultiEdit with a
#     *.rs matcher that dispatches RegisterTouch through the
#     storehouse bus + a Procfile worker that dispatches Sweep on
#     a 60s cadence.
#
#   * Phase 3 — The :exec / :claude_tool adapter binding for
#     LaunchConversion that actually fires `claude --headless` (or
#     the Agent-tool MCP) with the conversion prompt baked in and
#     cascades the sidequest's outcome (PR URL) back through
#     Cascade.RecordResult so CompleteConversion can close the loop.
#
# Memory-adapter backed for tests + behaviors ; once Phase 2 lands
# the .heki binary store will hold the working queues across sessions.
#
Hecks.hecksagon "RustToBluebookMacrophage" do
  adapter :memory
end
